<b><font size=4>SEARCH FOR AVAILABLE BACKGROUND DATA</font></b>
<p>
<b>Peter Goodwin</b><br>
<i>University of Idaho (UI), Boise</i>
<p>

UI met with River Masters Engineering to collect survey data and other background information related to the Red River Project. With this information, the initial ArcView GIS database is being created.
<p>
Gloria Beattie and Dave Fuhrman have also visited the USFS, Nez Perce Tribe, and CE Engineering in a preliminary assessment of available information for the Red River Restoration site and immediate watershed.
<p>
Dave Fuhrman initiated a literature survey for background information that can be used in the design of Phases III and IV of the current restoration project, as well as any future extensions of the project beyond the IDFG property

	</td>
	<td width="50%" valign="top">
	
<b><font size=4>WETLAND DELINEATION SURVEY</font></b>
<p>
<b>Rick Marbury and Gloria Beattie</b><br>
<i>University of Idaho (UI), Boise</i>
<p>
During June 10th - 14th Tom Duebendorfer, (wetland biologist for the project) performed the wetland delineation for Phase IV project area.
<p>
Over 800 points were surveyed during the week of June 22nd as part of the wetland delineation process.  The survey was undertaken using a Topcon Total Station and HP automated data logger.
<p>
The survey has been downloaded successfully and data points checked for consistency.  Preliminary maps have been prepared using ArcInfo.  The final maps and specific deliverables requested by Tom Duebendorfer will be completed in July

	</td>
